[23.784784, "o", "\u001b[36minfo\u001b[0m \u001b[2m[oss-license-non-empty]\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[2m\u00b7 LICENSE \u2014 LICENSE file is suspiciously short; paste the full license text rather than a stub. (no\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2mfixer)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36minfo\u001b[0m \u001b[2m[oss-security-policy-exists]\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[2m\u00b7 Consider adding a SECURITY.md so vulnerability reporters know where to disclose. (no fixer)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36minfo\u001b[0m \u001b[2m[oss-dependency-update-tool]\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[2m\u00b7 Consider configuring Dependabot or Renovate to keep dependencies and actions up to date. (no fixer)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36minfo\u001b[0m \u001b[2m[oss-codeowners-exists]\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[2m\u00b7 Consider adding a CODEOWNERS file so PR reviews are auto-routed. (no fixer)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36minfo\u001b[0m \u001b[2m[oss-code-of-conduct-exists]\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[2m\u00b7 Consider adding a CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md. (no fixer)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36minfo\u001b[0m \u001b[2m[oss-gitignore-exists]\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[2m\u00b7 Most OSS repos should have a .gitignore to keep build artefacts and secrets out of git. (no fixer)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36minfo\u001b[0m \u001b[2m[oss-final-newline]\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[32m\u2713 Cargo.toml \u2014 appended final newline to Cargo.toml\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36minfo\u001b[0m \u001b[2m[oss-no-trailing-whitespace]\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[32m\u2713 Cargo.toml \u2014 trimmed trailing whitespace in Cargo.toml\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[32m\u2713 README.md \u2014 trimmed trailing whitespace in README.md\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[33mwarning\u001b[0m \u001b[2m[rust-cargo-lock-exists]\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[2m\u00b7 Committing Cargo.lock ensures reproducible builds for binary crates. Library-only workspaces may\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2mlegitimately opt out; set this rule's `level: off` in that case. (no fixer)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36minfo\u001b[0m \u001b[2m[rust-toolchain-pinned]\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[2m\u00b7 Pinning a toolchain (rust-toolchain.toml) makes local and CI builds reproducible. (no fixer)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36minfo\u001b[0m \u001b[2m[rust-sources-no-trailing-whitespace]\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[32m\u2713 crates/core/src/lib.rs \u2014 trimmed trailing whitespace in crates/core/src/lib.rs\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[31merror\u001b[0m \u001b[2m[node-package-json-exists]\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[2m\u00b7 Node project: package.json at the root is required. (no fixer)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[33mwarning\u001b[0m \u001b[2m[node-has-lockfile]\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[2m\u00b7 A lockfile should be committed (package-lock.json / pnpm-lock.yaml / yarn.lock / bun.lock). (no fixer)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36minfo\u001b[0m \u001b[2m[node-engine-or-nvmrc]\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[2m\u00b7 Pin the Node.js version with `.nvmrc`, `.node-version`, or `.tool-versions` so local and CI installs\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2mmatch. (no fixer)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[31merror\u001b[0m \u001b[2m[python-manifest-exists]\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[2m\u00b7 Python project: a `pyproject.toml` (preferred), `setup.py`, or `setup.cfg` at the repo root is required.\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m(no fixer)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[33mwarning\u001b[0m \u001b[2m[python-has-lockfile]\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[2m\u00b7 A lockfile should be committed for reproducible installs (uv.lock / poetry.lock / Pipfile.lock /\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2mpdm.lock). (no fixer)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36minfo\u001b[0m \u001b[2m[python-sources-no-trailing-whitespace]\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[32m\u2713 services/svc/handler.py \u2014 trimmed trailing whitespace in services/svc/handler.py\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[33mwarning\u001b[0m \u001b[2m[gha-workflow-contents-read]\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[2m\u00b7 .github/workflows/ci.yml \u2014 GitHub workflows should declare `permissions.contents: read` at the\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2mworkflow level. Workflows that truly need write can override this rule or set per-job permissions. (no\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2mfixer)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[33mwarning\u001b[0m \u001b[2m[gha-pin-actions-to-sha]\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[2m\u00b7 .github/workflows/ci.yml \u2014 Third-party action is not pinned to a commit SHA. Pin with `@<40-char-sha>\u001b[0m\r\n    \u001b[2m# v4.1.1` so a compromised tag can't silently change what runs. (no fixer)\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[32m5 applied\u001b[0m, 0 skipped, 15 unfixable.\r\n"]
